-- title:
--   Transfer-matrix weight tables for Hollom's hypergraph
-- statement:
--   After all six hyperedges of Hollom's hypergraph have been swept, the transfer matrix of `BunkbedTransfer` has exactly **47** reachable states, out of the $B_5 = 52$ partitions of a five-element set. `stFinal` lists those 47 profiles and `wFinal` records, for each one, the total weight of the level configurations realising it.
--
--   Each weight is a homogeneous polynomial of degree $6$ — one factor per hyperedge — in the four Wierman--Ziff state probabilities $x = P_{abc}$, $y = P_{a|b|c}$, $z = P_{a|bc}$ and $u = P_{ab|c} = P_{ac|b}$, the last two being identified in the symmetric case. Together these 47 polynomials are exactly what the six-step dynamic programme computes in place of the $5^6$ individual level configurations; the largest of them has 51 monomials.
-- source:
--   Gladkov, Pak, Zimin, *The bunkbed conjecture is false*, PNAS 122 (2025) no. 24, e2420725122; Section 3, Hollom's 3-uniform hypergraph (Fig. 1) and the path $\rho$ of Eq. [5].

import Definitions.Def_BunkbedTransfer

/-!
# The transfer-matrix weight tables for Hollom's hypergraph

After all six hyperedges the transfer matrix of `Def_BunkbedTransfer` has exactly `47`
reachable states. `stFinal` lists them and `wFinal` records, for each one, the total weight
of the level configurations realising it: a homogeneous polynomial of degree `6` in
`x = P_abc`, `y = P_a|b|c`, `z = P_a|bc`, `u = P_ab|c = P_ac|b`. These 47 polynomials are what
the six-step dynamic programme computes in place of the `5 ^ 6` individual configurations.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace Bunkbed.TM

open Bunkbed.Hyper

